Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.4. Evaluation of Acquisition Proposals. <omitted> (f) During the Evaluation Period, the Company Board may decide on an Acquisition Proposal if, and only if, <omitted> (iii) the Company Board, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and financial advisor, determines in good faith that the failure to consider the Acquisition Proposal would be inconsistent with its fiduciary duties under applicable Law, (iv) the Company provides Parent with a written notice of the Board's intention to proceed with the Acquisition Proposal not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the third Business Day after Parent receives such notice and (v) if the Acquisition Proposal is not related to an Intervening Event under Section 8.4(g), the decision to proceed is based on a combination of financial terms and the strategic benefits as assessed by the Board, and the Company has complied with clauses (1) through (4), as follows: (1) the Company Board must have determined that the Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company has shared with Parent the material terms and conditions of the Acquisition Proposal in both oral and written form, (3) the Company has negotiated in good faith with Parent during the three Business Day period provided in clause (iv) to amend the terms of the Agreement so that the Acquisition Proposal no longer qualifies as a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and the advice from its legal counsel and financial advisor, the Company Board determines in good faith that the Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and not proceeding with the Acquisition Proposal would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law. Any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal will require a new notice period of two Business Days. (Pages 88-89)\nAnswer:
Choices:

